# Price-time FIFO: A's 10 units fill first, then 2 of B's 7.
submit 1 A 1 buy 100 10
submit 2 B 2 buy 100 7
submit 3 D 3 sell 100 12
# Same-price reduction, followed by cancellation.
replace 4 B 2 100 4
cancel 5 B 2
# C has a maximum position of 10 and 1000 cash.
submit 6 C 4 buy 100 11
submit 7 C 5 buy 100 8
submit 8 C 6 buy 100 5
cancel 9 C 5
submit 10 C 7 buy 100 5
# Kill switch blocks new exposure and permits cancellation.
kill 11 on
submit 12 A 8 buy 99 1
cancel 13 C 7
kill 14 off
# Crossing executes at the resting price, with partial fill/replacement.
submit 15 D 9 sell 103 5
submit 16 A 10 buy 104 3
replace 17 D 9 102 4
submit 18 B 11 buy 102 4
# Unknown cancellation and self-crossing are explicit rejections.
cancel 19 B 999
submit 20 A 12 buy 98 1
submit 21 A 13 sell 98 1
cancel 22 A 12
